      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The delay you're experiencing is due to DNS propagation, which is essentially the time it takes for all the world's DNS servers to update their records. Think of it like a massive, slow-moving stampede of information across the internet. While you've updated the A records, not every server has checked the latest information yet. It's a global process, and it can take anywhere from a few minutes to 48 hours for everything to catch up.",
