    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. is there anything i can do on my end to speed it up though? like is there a specific setting in the dns config that makes it update faster?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Unfortunately, you can't directly force the entire global DNS system to update faster, as that's controlled by caching resolvers all over the internet. You can, however, check the Time To Live (TTL) setting on your old records, as a very high TTL tells the world's servers to hold onto the old IP address for a long time. If you set a low TTL *before* making the change, it tells them to check for updates more frequently, which can help speed up the process when you finally push the new IP.",
